        "sensor_height_cm": 200,
        "note": "The scout car of 16b cut AE.1: the stock tank's five sections cut down, with a pair of wheels where the tracks were and the machine gun as its only gun until cut AE.2 gives it its autocannon. 3,000 cm/s is 108 kph on a road, which the wheeled row prices at 80; on grass (220) the terrain factor holds it to about 1,360 cm/s against the stock tank's 1,153, so it is quicker than a tank anywhere it can go. What it pays is where it can go: rubble, rock and the thick woods refuse it, a slope past 25 per cent refuses it where a tank climbs 45, and it fords at 400, five times a road, since the water row moved. Its ceiling on an 80 road is 3,000 x 100 / 80 = 3,750 cm/s, under the 3,996 that would shorten the 250 ms substep. The wheels are a pair: one gone is slow(50) and no turn toward it, both gone is disable_motion. The armour is half the tank's: 200 on the bow is two 105 rounds. VERSION 2 (16b cut AE.2): the 30 mm autocannon in the turret, first in component order, so it is the bare FIRE."
